nodes.prompt:
Coding goal: {{goal}}

Split this goal into steps only when it is big: it asks for several separate things (a list of improvements, several features, a change across many areas). A goal that is one change, one fix or one feature in one area is not big.
Answer with one JSON object and no other text: { "milestones": [ "step one", "step two" ] }
For a goal that is not big the list is empty. For a big goal it has 2 to 8 steps, in the order they should be done. Each step is one sentence that stands alone (everything it refers to written out), names the part of the project it touches, and is small enough to be done and built in one go; the project builds after every step. Never list a step that only reads or plans, and never a step the goal did not ask for: do not widen the goal (not "everywhere", not "all of them", unless it says so).

